    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d710">

                <pb facs="0790" n="710" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg710"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hill to Mr. Buck.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-04-14"><hi rendition="#italic">April 14,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 400.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    dispatch No. 027, of the 18th ultimo, confirming your telegram of the preceding
                    night in relation to the proposal of the Japanese Government to arbitrate the
                    question of the tax on buildings erected on lands held by perpetual leases in
                    the former foreign settlements in Japan.</p>
                <p>The Department approves your view that you ought not to ask that the United
                    States be included as one of the powers to participate in the arbitration
                    proceedings, unless so instructed.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">David J. Hill</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
